e was injured early in 1936 and, although he tried to make the American team, was not the runner he had been in 1935."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The 1936 Olympics were a showcase for Jesse Owens, who won four gold medals, the 100, " [:a {:href "/results/58166"} "200"] ", " [:a {:href "/results/58318"} "long jump"] ", and on the " [:a {:href "/results/58263"} "4x100 relay"] ". Further, in front the " [:a {:href "/athletes/1100010"} "Adolf Hitler"] " and the Nazi regime, he shattered their myths of Aryan supremacy."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "QF"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "733"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78869"} "Jesse Owens"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "10.3 (1 h12)"] [:td {} "10.2w (1 h2)"] [:td {} "10.4 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "10.3w (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "732"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78787"} "Ralph Metcalfe"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "10.8 (1 h7)"] [:td {} "10.5 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "10.5 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "10.4w (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "299"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/73863"} "Tinus Osendarp"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NED"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NED.png"}] "NED"]] [:td {} "10.5 (1 h10)"] [:td {} "10.6 (2 h1)"] [:td 